class_name SceneGraph
extends Object

# Which way from here to there, across the whole world.
#
# GENERATED by tools/gen_scenegraph.py. Do not edit by hand -- regenerate.
#
# The quest arrow has to answer "which way?" from any of two hundred scenes to
# any other. Parsing .tscn at runtime to find out is far too slow, and a
# hand-written map would be wrong within a week: tools/check_doors.py exists
# because doors drift. So the graph is generated from the same doors the game
# loads, and carries each door's position, so the arrow can point at the
# doorway rather than vaguely across the street.
#
# Doors a scene builds in code -- the hotel corridor makes one per room -- are
# absent and cannot be present: they do not exist until the scene runs. Those
# floors are leaves, so nothing routes through them.
#
# A door marked is_return leads wherever the player came in from, which is not
# a fixed edge and is left out for the same reason.

